# Copy to .env.development.local for `npm run dev`. Only `npm run dev` uses that file.
#
# The admin login (ADMIN_EMAIL, ADMIN_PASSWORD, LOCAL_SESSION_SECRET) does NOT go in any .env file. OpenNext copies
# every .env file into the Worker it builds, and the build stops if one holds those names. Put the login in .dev.vars
# instead: `npm run dev` and `npm run preview` both read it, and nothing is built from it. On Cloudflare the login is
# three Worker secrets (GO-LIVE.md, step 5).

# Public addresses, fixed into the pages when the site is built. The defaults are the live addresses, so a production
# build needs neither line (GO-LIVE.md, step 7). Here, for this computer only:
#   the site's own address, used for canonical links, the sitemap and share images
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
#   where every Lair link goes (they open in a new tab); default https://interactive.nihaalnazeer.com/?film=on
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LAIR_URL=http://localhost:4700/?film=on&site=local

# Optional: Supabase as the content store instead of local mode. The live site doesn't use it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY belongs in .dev.vars, never here; only `npm run cms:push` uses it.
